text:
That kills my hypothesis outright. `do_delete_pet` already does the right thing:

```c
velapaw_store_delete(id);            /* history + BCS, shifted to match */
velapaw_identity_delete(id);         /* the pet itself + icon, renumbers rest */
```

plus it shifts all four of its own per-pet meal tables and invalidates every held id. And [identity.h:52-56](apps/examples/velapaw/identity/identity.h#L52) documents the renumbering hazard explicitly and names the exact functions that must shift. The index-aliasing bug I predicted was anticipated and handled.

Which also dissolves the data-corruption worry. `count == 1` because three pets were deleted through the UI, their history shifted out correctly, and `bob,`'s 38 g/day baseline and 298 g week total are his own — drawn from history.bin, which holds 30 days, while `feed_log.md` is size-capped and restarts (`st.st_size > VP_LOG_MAX` → reopen with `"w"`). The log we read is just the latest fragment. Nothing is orphaned and no food is misattributed.

So the honest tally after reading the code: **four of my hypotheses failed and two real defects stand.**

## Defect 1 — the clock anchor (one line)

```c
-#define VELAPAW_CLOCK_ANCHOR 1788393600L           /* 2026-09-03 00:00 */
+#define VELAPAW_CLOCK_ANCHOR 1791676800L           /* 2026-10-11 00:00 */
```

at [ui_lvgl.c:3620](apps/examples/velapaw/ui/ui_lvgl.c#L3620). This is the unambiguous one: the board sets itself to 2026-09-03 **08:00** on every cold boot, so morning meals read as due every single power-up — that's the unprompted `dispensed 3 pocket(s) ~15g` we watched — and the 30-day window can never roll, because `vp_sync_day` sees `today <= g_hist_day` and correctly refuses to go backwards.

## Defect 2 — name trim at the single write site

`bob,` and `  bob` are genuinely in flash. Both format strings are clean, so the junk is stored. It breaks the markdown heading in status.md and would let one animal hold two identities with two daily limits.

Replace the two lines at [identity.c:276](apps/examples/velapaw/identity/identity.c#L276):

```c
/* Names arrive from the enroll dialog and from seeded demo data, where a
 * delimiter can still be attached ("bob," / "  bob").  Ids are array
 * indices, but the NAME is what every report keys on visually, so junk
 * here becomes a broken heading in status.md and makes one animal look
 * like two.  Trim once, at the only place a name is stored.
 */
static void vp_copy_name(char *dst, size_t cap, const char *src)
{
  size_t n;

  if (src == NULL)
    {
      src = "pet";
    }

  while (*src == ' ' || *src == '\t')
    {
      src++;
    }

  n = strnlen(src, cap - 1);
  while (n > 0 && strchr(" \t,;.", src[n - 1]) != NULL)
    {
      n--;
    }

  if (n == 0)
    {
      n = 3;
      src = "pet";
    }

  memcpy(dst, src, n);
  dst[n] = '\0';
}
```

then at the call site:

```c
-  strncpy(p->name, name ? name : "pet", VELAPAW_NAME_MAX - 1);
-  p->name[VELAPAW_NAME_MAX - 1] = '\0';
+  vp_copy_name(p->name, VELAPAW_NAME_MAX, name);
```

That fixes new enrollments. The existing `bob,` record is already in flash, so either re-enroll him or run the same trim across loaded records in `velapaw_identity_load()` — the latter heals the board without touching the UI, and I'd do it, since it costs four lines in a loop you already have.

## Before building

Both files are in subtrees with the duplicate-object pattern, so for each one:

```sh
cd ~/openvela/apps/examples/velapaw
rm -f ui/ui_lvgl.c.*.o identity/identity.c.*.o
rm -f .built .depend Make.dep
```

then `./build.sh esp32s3-devkit:waveshare_lcd -j4` from `~/openvela`.

## One open question

Who called `velapaw_identity_enroll` with a comma attached? Worth knowing before we assume the trim is sufficient:

```sh
cd ~/openvela/apps/examples/velapaw
grep -rn "velapaw_identity_enroll" --include=*.c . | head
```

If it's only the UI dialog, the trim is the whole fix. If there's a seed path splitting a literal like `"jay,  bob, king"`, that splitter wants fixing too.

Recorded. Here's the complete fix set.

## Patch 1 — the anchor (the one worth flashing for)

[ui_lvgl.c:3620](apps/examples/velapaw/ui/ui_lvgl.c#L3620)

```c
-#define VELAPAW_CLOCK_ANCHOR 1788393600L           /* 2026-09-03 00:00 */
+#define VELAPAW_CLOCK_ANCHOR 1791676800L           /* 2026-10-11 00:00 */
```

**Expect the window to wipe on the first boot after this, and that's correct.** `vp_sync_day()` will see a forward delta of 38 days, clamp it to `DAYS` (30), and shift the entire window out — which flushes the synthetic enrollment seed that every baseline and appetite % has been computed against. status.md will come back with 0 g baselines until real days accumulate. That's the honest state replacing a fake one, and it's exactly what memory says the write-up must not claim as learned.

## Patch 2 — name trim at the single write site

Add above `velapaw_identity_init()` in [identity.c](apps/examples/velapaw/identity/identity.c):

```c
/* The on-screen enroll keyboard admits a stray comma or a double space, and
 * this is the only place a name becomes persistent -- so trim here and the
 * dialog, the CLI and any future agent tool are all covered at once.  Junk
 * lands in status.md as a broken markdown heading and makes one animal look
 * like two distinct keys.
 */
static void vp_copy_name(char *dst, size_t cap, const char *src)
{
  size_t n;

  if (src == NULL)
    {
      src = "pet";
    }

  while (*src == ' ' || *src == '\t')
    {
      src++;
    }

  n = strnlen(src, cap - 1);
  while (n > 0 && strchr(" \t,;.", src[n - 1]) != NULL)
    {
      n--;
    }

  if (n == 0)
    {
      src = "pet";
      n   = 3;
    }

  memcpy(dst, src, n);
  dst[n] = '\0';
}
```

Replace the store at `identity.c:276`:

```c
-  strncpy(p->name, name ? name : "pet", VELAPAW_NAME_MAX - 1);
-  p->name[VELAPAW_NAME_MAX - 1] = '\0';
+  vp_copy_name(p->name, VELAPAW_NAME_MAX, name);
```

And heal what's already in flash — immediately after the existing `velapaw_identity_load()` call at `identity.c:237`:

```c
   velapaw_identity_load();      /* bring back previously enrolled pets + icons */
+
+  /* Records enrolled before the trim existed keep their junk in flash.
+   * Fix them in place and persist once, only if something changed.
+   */
+  bool fixed = false;
+  for (int i = 0; i < g_npets; i++)
+    {
+      char tmp[VELAPAW_NAME_MAX];
+
+      vp_copy_name(tmp, sizeof(tmp), g_pets[i].name);
+      if (strcmp(tmp, g_pets[i].name) != 0)
+        {
+          memcpy(g_pets[i].name, tmp, sizeof(tmp));
+          fixed = true;
+        }
+    }
+
+  if (fixed)
+    {
+      velapaw_identity_save();
+    }
```

## Build

Both files sit in subtrees with the duplicate-object pattern, so:

```sh
cd ~/openvela/apps/examples/velapaw
rm -f ui/ui_lvgl.c.*.o identity/identity.c.*.o
rm -f .built .depend Make.dep
cd ~/openvela && ./build.sh esp32s3-devkit:waveshare_lcd -j4
```

## Pass criteria after flashing

1. **No `[feeder] dispensed ... pocket(s)` line during boot** — that's the real fix landing.
2. `ask read me /data/ai_agent/velapaw/feed_log.md verbatim and nothing else` shows timestamps dated **2026-10-11** and advancing monotonically.
3. status.md's heading reads `## bob` with no comma, and baselines read 0 g.

Criterion 1 is the one that matters — it's the difference between a feeder that gives away food on every power cycle and one that doesn't.

Fair — here they are as one applicable patch. I dropped the in-place name healing from code: it needed an edit inside `velapaw_identity_init()`, whose surrounding lines I haven't read, and the only affected record is one pet. Deleting and re-enrolling `bob,` through the UI fixes it with zero code risk, and the trim stops it recurring.

Write the patch on the VM:

```sh
cd ~/openvela/apps/examples/velapaw
cat > /tmp/velapaw-clock-and-names.patch <<'PATCH_EOF'
--- a/ui/ui_lvgl.c
+++ b/ui/ui_lvgl.c
@@ -3620 +3620 @@
-#define VELAPAW_CLOCK_ANCHOR 1788393600L           /* 2026-09-03 00:00 */
+#define VELAPAW_CLOCK_ANCHOR 1791676800L           /* 2026-10-11 00:00 */
--- a/identity/identity.c
+++ b/identity/identity.c
@@ -240,4 +240,40 @@
+/* The on-screen enroll keyboard admits a stray comma or a double space, and
+ * this is the only place a name becomes persistent, so trimming here covers
+ * the dialog, the CLI and any future agent tool at once.  Junk in a name
+ * lands in status.md as a broken markdown heading and makes one animal look
+ * like two distinct keys.
+ */
+static void vp_copy_name(char *dst, size_t cap, const char *src)
+{
+  size_t n;
+
+  if (src == NULL)
+    {
+      src = "pet";
+    }
+
+  while (*src == ' ' || *src == '\t')
+    {
+      src++;
+    }
+
+  n = strnlen(src, cap - 1);
+  while (n > 0 && strchr(" \t,;.", src[n - 1]) != NULL)
+    {
+      n--;
+    }
+
+  if (n == 0)
+    {
+      src = "pet";
+      n   = 3;
+    }
+
+  memcpy(dst, src, n);
+  dst[n] = '\0';
+}
+
 int velapaw_identity_count(void)
 {
   return g_npets;
 }
@@ -272,9 +308,8 @@
   for (int k = 0; k < VELAPAW_MAX_MEALS; k++)
     {
       p->meal_min[k] = meal_min ? meal_min[k] : -1;
     }
-  strncpy(p->name, name ? name : "pet", VELAPAW_NAME_MAX - 1);
-  p->name[VELAPAW_NAME_MAX - 1] = '\0';
+  vp_copy_name(p->name, VELAPAW_NAME_MAX, name);

   /* Average the sample embeddings. */
   for (int d = 0; d < VELAPAW_EMBED_DIM; d++)
PATCH_EOF
patch -p1 --dry-run < /tmp/velapaw-clock-and-names.patch
```

If the dry run reports both files patching cleanly, apply it:

```sh
cd ~/openvela/apps/examples/velapaw
patch -p1 < /tmp/velapaw-clock-and-names.patch
grep -n "VELAPAW_CLOCK_ANCHOR 17" ui/ui_lvgl.c
grep -n "vp_copy_name" identity/identity.c
```

Expect `1791676800L` on the first and two hits on the second — the definition and the call.

I used a zero-context hunk for the anchor because I've only read lines 3618–3625 individually, not the comment block around them, so I can't supply trustworthy context. `patch` accepts that; `git apply` would need `--unidiff-zero`. If that hunk is the only one rejected, this is whitespace-independent:

```sh
sed -i 's/^#define VELAPAW_CLOCK_ANCHOR [0-9]*L.*$/#define VELAPAW_CLOCK_ANCHOR 1791676800L           \/* 2026-10-11 00:00 *\//' ui/ui_lvgl.c
```

Then build, clearing both object variants:

```sh
cd ~/openvela/apps/examples/velapaw
rm -f ui/ui_lvgl.c.*.o identity/identity.c.*.o .built .depend Make.dep
cd ~/openvela && ./build.sh esp32s3-devkit:waveshare_lcd -j4
```

Watch for `CC: ui/ui_lvgl.c` and `CC: identity/identity.c` in the output — their absence is the stale-object trap, not a successful no-op build.

