Before you run script 2: **it has an escaping bug, don't use the version above.** Inside a quoted heredoc bash passes the text through untouched, so my `'\\n'` and `\\w` reach Python as literal backslash sequences rather than a newline and a regex class. It fails loudly at the `re.search` (prints `FAIL could not find the tool_cron.h include` and stops) rather than corrupting anything, but it won't finish. Corrected version — same content, single backslashes, and the line insertions now use real newlines instead of escapes:

